93 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 239 0 R
/E (3D Graphic Rendering Using Matrix Chain Multiplication is a project that focuses on optimizing matrix operations involved in 3D graphics. Various transformation matrices such as translation, rotation, scaling, and projection are required to render and transform 3D objects. Multiplying these matrices in an inefficient order can increase computational cost. This project uses the Matrix Chain Multiplication algorithm with Dynamic Programming to determine the optimal order of matrix multiplication while minimizing the number of scalar multiplications. The system calculates the minimum computational cost and displays the optimal parenthesization of the matrix chain. This approach helps reduce unnecessary calculations, improves computational efficiency, and demonstrates how Data Structures and Algorithms can be applied to real-world computer graphics and rendering applications.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
